{"route":"/docs/6.0/utilities/pointer-events/","version":"6.0","renderedVersion":"6.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Pointer events","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Control how elements respond to mouse and touch interactions with pointer-events utilities."},"blocks":[{"id":"content--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","scope":"col","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Class"}]},{"type":"th","scope":"col","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Styles"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":".pe-none"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"pointer-events: none;"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":".pe-auto"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"pointer-events: auto;"}]}]}]},{"id":"overview","type":"heading","en":"Overview","level":2},{"id":"overview--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap provides <code>.pe-none</code> and <code>.pe-auto</code> classes to prevent or add element interactions through the <code>pointer-events</code> CSS property."},{"id":"basic-usage","type":"heading","en":"Basic usage","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage--example-1","type":"demo","key":"24d8389bca545ecd396e","height":201},{"id":"basic-usage--code-1","type":"code","value":"<p><a href=\"#\" class=\"pe-none\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-disabled=\"true\">This link</a> can not be clicked.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#\" class=\"pe-auto\">This link</a> can be clicked (this is default behavior).</p>\n<p class=\"pe-none\"><a href=\"#\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-disabled=\"true\">This link</a> can not be clicked because the <code>pointer-events</code> property is inherited from its parent. However, <a href=\"#\" class=\"pe-auto\">this link</a> has a <code>pe-auto</code> class and can be clicked.</p>","language":""},{"id":"important-considerations","type":"heading","en":"Important considerations","level":2},{"id":"important-considerations--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The <code>.pe-none</code> class (and the <code>pointer-events</code> CSS property it sets) only prevents interactions with a pointer (mouse, stylus, touch). Links and controls with <code>.pe-none</code> are, by default, still focusable and actionable for keyboard users."},{"id":"important-considerations--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"To ensure that they are completely neutralized even for keyboard users, you may need to add further attributes such as:"},{"id":"important-considerations--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"important-considerations--item-1","type":"item","en":"<code>tabindex=&quot;-1&quot;</code> (to prevent them from receiving keyboard focus)"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"important-considerations--item-2","type":"item","en":"<code>aria-disabled=&quot;true&quot;</code> (to convey the fact they are effectively disabled to assistive technologies)"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"important-considerations--item-3","type":"item","en":"JavaScript to completely prevent them from being actionable"}]}]},{"id":"better-alternatives","type":"heading","en":"Better alternatives","level":2},{"id":"better-alternatives--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"If possible, the simpler solution is:"},{"id":"better-alternatives--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"better-alternatives--item-1","type":"item","en":"<strong>For form controls</strong>: Add the <code>disabled</code> HTML attribute"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"better-alternatives--item-2","type":"item","en":"<strong>For links</strong>: Remove the <code>href</code> attribute, making it a non-interactive anchor or placeholder link"}]}]},{"id":"better-alternatives--note-1","type":"note","tone":"warning","body":[{"id":"better-alternatives--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>Accessibility warning:</strong> Using <code>pointer-events: none</code> can create accessibility barriers. Always ensure that disabled elements are properly marked up with appropriate ARIA attributes and that keyboard users can’t accidentally focus them."}]},{"id":"use-cases","type":"heading","en":"Use cases","level":2},{"id":"use-cases--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"use-cases--item-1","type":"item","en":"<strong><code>.pe-none</code></strong> - Disable interactions on overlays, loading states, or temporarily disabled elements"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"use-cases--item-2","type":"item","en":"<strong><code>.pe-auto</code></strong> - Re-enable interactions on child elements when parent has <code>pe-none</code>"}]}]},{"id":"css","type":"heading","en":"CSS","level":2},{"id":"sass-utilities-api","type":"heading","en":"Sass utilities API","level":3},{"id":"sass-utilities-api--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Pointer events utilities are declared in our utilities API in <code>scss/_utilities.scss</code>. <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/api#using-the-api\">Learn how to use the utilities API.</a>"},{"id":"sass-utilities-api--code-1","type":"code","value":"\"pointer-events\": (\n  property: pointer-events,\n  class: pe,\n  values: none auto,\n),","language":""}],"demos":[{"key":"24d8389bca545ecd396e","html":"<p><a href=\"#\" class=\"pe-none\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-disabled=\"true\">This link</a> can not be clicked.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#\" class=\"pe-auto\">This link</a> can be clicked (this is default behavior).</p>\n<p class=\"pe-none\"><a href=\"#\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-disabled=\"true\">This link</a> can not be clicked because the <code>pointer-events</code> property is inherited from its parent. However, <a href=\"#\" class=\"pe-auto\">this link</a> has a <code>pe-auto</code> class and can be clicked.</p>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}